<!--
    The launcher icon: the owner's pixel portrait, 90x90 cells, nine colours.

    ── Framed for the MASK, not for the canvas ────────────────────────────────────
    Both adaptive-icon layers are 108dp. The launcher's mask crops that to a 72dp
    visible area, and only the centred 66dp CIRCLE is guaranteed to survive every
    mask shape. The icon this replaces was drawn to fit INSIDE that 66dp circle,
    which is why it looked small with empty ground around it on a round launcher
    (reported from the phone, 2026-08-11).

    So the drawing BLEEDS instead: the bust runs off the left, right and bottom of
    the 108dp canvas and is cut by whatever mask the launcher applies, while the
    only thing kept inside the 66dp circle is the HEAD - the part that must never
    be clipped. The head's furthest corner sits 32.95dp from the centre.

    ── Reproducing it ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Source: a 90x90 pixel drawing. Cell -> dp: x*1.15 + 9.725, y*1.15 + 13.000,
    chosen so the head's centre column lands on the canvas centre and the top of
    the hair sits at y=22.2. Same-coloured cells are merged into maximal rectangles;
    201 of them across 7 paths. Nothing here is hand-tuned - change the
    numbers above and regenerate, do not nudge a path.

    The dark ground is NOT drawn here: it is the background layer
    (@color/ic_launcher_background), so the mask never exposes an edge.
-->
